### 🟡 MEDIUM

#### 5. Eager Test
**File:** `OrderProcessorTests.cs` · **Method:** `OrderProcessor_FullWorkflow_Succeeds` (lines 57–63)

```csharp
processor.ValidateOrder(order);
processor.CalculateTotal(order);
processor.ApplyDiscount(order, "SAVE10");
processor.ReserveInventory(order);
processor.ProcessPayment(order, new CreditCard("4111111111111111"));
processor.SendConfirmation(order);
processor.UpdateOrderHistory(order);
```

7 distinct production methods called. A failure in any one makes diagnosis ambiguous. **Fix:** break into per-step unit tests; if a full-workflow test is wanted, mark it `[TestCategory("Integration")]` and assert intermediate states.

**Risk if unfixed:** Hard-to-diagnose failures; changes to any step break a single monolithic test.

